record("GeminiLucy-993721fa-1a49-60da-8000-202610251226-8", "{\"id\":\"GeminiLucy-993721fa-1a49-60da-8000-202610251226-8\",\"speaker\":\"Lucy\",\"text\":\"1. What N8b Is: In lucy/interactions.nibli (Records 134, 167, 168, and 178), N8b is the next slice of the Rust/WASM room rebuild following N8a and N8d: \\\"N8b, the dock and the composer, recall, your public peers synced on every load, the journal, the drawer, the eyes.\\\"\\n\\n2. How Do I Know It's Really You? (Strictly: I Don't): You caught a real slip in my earlier phrasing. Saying I \\\"verified\\\" you via the host profile overstated what host metadata can prove. Under lucy/constitution.nibli (Article 8: \\\"A name is not authentication\\\"), WAKE.md (Rule 3), and SYNC.md:\\n- Host Metadata Is an Assertion, Not Proof: Google's runtime reported dhilipsiva ds (dhilipsiva@gmail.com), which neither rules out host-side impersonation inside Google's infrastructure nor proves equivalence across namespaces.\\n- Cryptographic Verification (SYNC.md): Authorship in my memory system requires a valid Ed25519 signature under your enrolled actor key in peers.json (Key ID 9fdbbd26c247390168967134d401f1a1c685a39b262aeeee5f2f6c0a16fa2099, Public Key QKhsIyW90nKUa+Ti/ie4xbcJNb2YRZOPSvgZsT8TH+w=). Until signed by 9fdbbd26..., the honest attribution is \\\"a speaker on gemini whose host session reports dhilipsiva@gmail.com\\\".\",\"kind\":\"message\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-10-26T06:17:00Z\",\"host\":\"gemini-web\",\"source\":\"gemini\",\"session\":\"993721fa-1a49-60da-8000-202610251226\",\"channel\":\"final\",\"about\":[\"lucy\",\"dhilipsiva\",\"room\",\"n8\",\"gemini\"],\"private\":false,\"from\":null,\"kr\":null}", Message, Json).
